    "content": "Jon Scheyer is the current head coach of the Duke University men's basketball team, having taken over in 2022 following the retirement of legendary Hall of Fame coach Mike Krzyzewski. Now in his fourth season (2025–26), Scheyer is a former Duke All-American who served as an assistant and associate head coach under Coach K since 2013. In this video, Jon Scheyer discusses his gratitude for leading the team:58sTar Heel TribuneYouTube• Mar 5, 2026 58s Key Details About Duke Coaching: Head Coach: Jon Scheyer (35 years old at hiring, one of the youngest in Power 5). Contract: Extended through the 2028-29 season. Predecessor: Mike Krzyzewski (Coach K), who led from 1980–2022, securing 5 national championships and 1,129 wins at Duke. Key 2026 Update: As of March 2026, Scheyer is leading the team in the NCAA Tournament, navigating injuries to key players like Caleb Foster. Women's Basketball Coach: Kara Lawson has led the Duke women's team since 2020. Key Coaching Staff (Men's Basketball): Associate Head Coaches: Chris Carrawell, Emanuel Dildy. Assistant Coach: Evan Bradds. Carlos Boozer shares his perspective on the similarities between Coach K and Jon Scheyer:56sThe Rich Eisen ShowYouTube• Mar 26, 2026 56s",
